WEBVTT

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.440
Well, if it ain't the legendary Urashimako himself!

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:11.150
What's wrong? Whatcha sighin' for?

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:14.110
Nothing. It's just Momiji.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.990
Momiji? Ya mean that God o' Misfortune?

00:00:16.990 --> 00:00:19.540
She got ya whipped again, boy?

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:24.250
Yeah. She wanted to turn some human named Sakura Ichiko into an old woman

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:27.000
with one of Otohime's Aging Boxes so she could take her Fortune,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.960
but I messed up and she got
turned into a kid instead.

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.300
She got away somehow and hid at her classmate Tsuwabuki's house,

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.810
but Momiji found her and told me to get another Aging Box to turn her into an old hag.

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:44.480
Momiji went to their picnic and it looks like she caught Sakura Ichiko, and now all she needs is my Aging Box.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.440
They're all so heartless.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:48.690
That's why I was sighing.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:52.860
And now I've just gone and indirectly given a recap of last week's episode.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.030
Nothin' indirect about it...

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:28.000
Oi, Michiko!

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.710
She didn't fall down... Did she?

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:35.840
<i>You kiddin' me?</i>

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:55.190
<i>I made it!</i>

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.610
Michiko!

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.410
Oh, R-Rika.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:03.700
Thank goodness you're all right!

00:03:04.370 --> 00:03:04.950
Huh?

00:03:05.790 --> 00:03:08.620
H-Hey... Where's Keita?

00:03:08.620 --> 00:03:09.540
Huh?

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.870
He's not with you?

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.290
Ouch...

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.960
Damn, I fell a long way.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.590
It's a miracle I'm alive.

00:03:21.590 --> 00:03:22.760
Ouch!

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.260
Aw, damn it!

00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:31.270
I have to hurry up and find Michiko so I can get back to the others!

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.270
What am I gonna do about work tomorrow?

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.690
Are you sure?

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:41.030
The next bus isn't until morning.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:44.490
Yes, we'll wait until our brother comes back.

00:03:48.370 --> 00:03:49.750
Rika...

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:53.210
It'll be all right! He'll come back soon.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:57.460
If we left without him, Keita would be lonely.

00:03:57.460 --> 00:03:58.750
Right.

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:03.010
<i>Geez! What're you doing, Tsuwabuki?</i>

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:06.260
<i>Hurry up and get back here!</i>

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:13.230
N-No... Keita...

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:15.020
Now now, Mika...

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.230
He went away...

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:25.110
Keita went away, just like Mom and Dad!

00:04:25.450 --> 00:04:29.990
Don't be stupid, Mika! Keita would never just leave us!

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:33.540
Now Sorata's crying too!

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:34.540
Calm down, Ryuu!

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.710
I said, stop crying!

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:40.880
Stop it, Ryuu! Not you too...

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:44.380
Don't you start crying too!

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.260
Why aren't they coming back?!

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.020
Michiko, where are you going?

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:58.230
I'm going to find Keita.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:01.280
No! You'll get lost too!

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:03.530
I'll be fine.

00:05:03.530 --> 00:05:04.280
Huh?

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:07.030
I'll be fine, so just wait here.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.450
I'll find him...

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:12.330
I'll find Keita...

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:15.160
No matter what!

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.170
Michiko!

00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:21.380
Geez, what should I do?

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:23.510
Keita...

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:30.050
Should be safe here.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:33.770
I'll leave this with you.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:36.230
If anything happens, please call me!

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:40.110
So do I just blow it?

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:45.780
Blow, and I will come!

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:47.700
Did you call, Miss Ichiko?

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:49.620
Please, Momou!

00:05:49.620 --> 00:05:52.870
Can you find the person with the
same scent as this handkerchief?

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.410
Miss... This is a man's scent.

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:56.870
Can you do it or not?!

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.500
Easy as pie.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:05.380
<i>I finally get it... The source of my frustration.</i>

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:06.920
<i>Though I don't want to admit it.</i>

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:11.470
<i>Gourmet food, money, a big house...</i>

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:16.180
<i>I have so many things that you don't.</i>

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:19.060
<i>And yet, you have...</i>

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:23.860
You have everything I don't!

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.240
Momou! Did you find him?!

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.620
Tsuwabuki!

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:37.290
What're you doing?!

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:42.590
Are you stupid? You wanna die here?!

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:46.510
Wake up, Tsuwabuki! Damn it, wake up!

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:49.760
Your brothers and sisters are
waiting for you! They're crying!

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:51.510
How could their big brother die like this?!

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:55.470
What're those kids gonna do if you don't come back?!

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:59.390
You better not think I'm gonna give a shit!
I won't look after them! I'll abandon them!

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:02.400
So... So...

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:05.400
Open your eyes!

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:13.620
Don't grow a heart just yet.

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:17.370
You're wide open.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:24.880
You heartless bitch!

00:07:27.090 --> 00:07:32.010
I'm broke, so this tiny tube was all I could afford. It's all your fault!

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:37.010
But it should be enough to save one human on the brink of death.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:39.060
God of Misfortune...

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:39.930
That's right.

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:43.310
I'm a God of Misfortune, not the Grim Reaper.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:48.900
If someone died because I took some Fortune, I'd be more than fired.

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.990
Except you're always like,
"I'm gonna fucking kill you!" to me.

00:07:51.990 --> 00:07:55.660
Don't be like that, Icchi!
You're just so cute I can't resist!

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:57.580
On the other hand,

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:06.460
if you let Tsuwabuki die here, that means I'll be pulled away from the human world.

00:08:07.090 --> 00:08:07.800
That was quick.

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:13.720
Oh man, that was a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.930
Oh, please. You think I'm scared of <i>you</i>?

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:18.890
But if I let him die...

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:21.350
I'll just feel bad!

00:08:22.690 --> 00:08:23.850
I guess so...

00:08:24.850 --> 00:08:26.190
I guess so.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:39.080
Oh shit, it's morning!

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.500
Michiko...

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.630
You came for me?

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:47.750
Huh?

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.420
<i>It's not broken?</i>

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:53.380
<i>And the wound healed up?</i>

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.090
<i>Did I dream all that?</i>

00:08:57.510 --> 00:08:59.390
All right, let's go.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:05.350
<i>But how do I even get back from here?</i>

00:09:05.350 --> 00:09:06.020
Hm?

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:09.020
What is this?

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:17.450
Was this here before?

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.490
Should I just follow it?

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.330
Wow, I really made it back.

00:09:29.960 --> 00:09:32.300
Sorry I'm late.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.090
Keita!

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:47.940
Man, we didn't find shit!

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.310
What happened to that Dog God nose of yours?

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:53.820
Where'd you run off to last night, eh? Playing hookey?

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.900
Miss Ichiko called me!

00:09:55.900 --> 00:09:59.450
I don't even want to hear that from you,
Mister Hits-On-Anything-That-Moves!

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:04.160
But as of this morning, there's a new smell in the air.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:08.870
There's no mistake. Urashima Taro is in the human world.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.920
What's with this guy? Some kind of freak?

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:16.170
You a god or a pod, man?

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:19.890
It's him!

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:22.890
Get outta here, brats!

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:27.350
Thank you very much!
How can I ever thank you?

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:31.310
Don't worry about that.
Just hand over the Aging Box.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:34.400
Out of the frying pan and into the fire!

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:38.820
Miss! Miss Ichiko!

00:10:39.280 --> 00:10:41.240
Huh? Momou! What is it?

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:44.080
Worry no more! We've got the Aging Box.

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.370
Really?!

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.870
Michiko, let's go.

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.250
Okay!

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.920
Anyway, thanks. Now's not a good time, so find me later.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:55.250
Hey, Michiko, how long are you gonna stay at our place?

00:10:56.630 --> 00:11:01.760
<i>Trying to get rid of me, huh? Don't worry, kid.
I'll be out of your hair by tonight.</i>

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:05.430
You can stay as long as you want, Michiko.

00:11:05.430 --> 00:11:06.180
Yeah!

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:07.600
Huh?

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:12.100
You really did find Keita, after all. It's almost as though...

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:16.360
you're some kind of angel sent by God!

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:20.280
Huh? The hell are you saying?

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:23.120
<i>I'll admit it. Everything...</i>

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:27.620
<i>Everything I don't have is in this house.</i>

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:30.870
<i>But so what? Do I want that?</i>

00:11:32.330 --> 00:11:34.130
<i>Give me a break.</i>

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:37.590
<i>Why would someone as fortunate as me be jealous of someone else?</i>

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:40.380
<i>But hypothetically... Hypothetically!</i>

00:11:40.380 --> 00:11:49.640
<i>Even if I wanted to live like this,
that'd mean I'd have to stay in this form.</i>

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:51.640
<i>Right?</i>

00:11:58.780 --> 00:12:01.740
My real name is Sakura Ichiko.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:07.240
I'm sorry. Michiko doesn't exist.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:12.040
Huh? You're still awake?

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.880
Um... I'm going home.

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:17.170
At this time of night?

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:20.170
They're waiting for me.

00:12:20.170 --> 00:12:21.720
Who's waiting?

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:25.220
Um... Well...

00:12:25.590 --> 00:12:29.100
The truth is, I've had a crush on Ryuuta this whole time!

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:33.730
I wanted to be friends with him for a long time but never had the courage to talk to him!

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:38.690
But I'm actually moving to America tomorrow, and...

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:41.820
I'm sorry. I wish I could thank you properl—

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:42.900
Don't worry about that.

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:46.780
You saved me, didn't you, Michiko?

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:52.540
To be honest, I don't really know what happened 'cause I was unconscious...

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:58.130
But if it weren't for you,
I don't think I'd be here right now.

00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:05.510
Hey, at least say goodbye to Mika.

00:13:06.260 --> 00:13:09.390
But that'll just make everyone sad.

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:11.060
That so?

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:12.390
It's all right.

00:13:13.180 --> 00:13:14.770
We'll...

00:13:15.890 --> 00:13:17.560
We'll meet again soon.

00:13:22.280 --> 00:13:25.530
You can come out now.

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:26.820
Ah ho ho!

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:27.740
Here, Princess!

00:13:27.740 --> 00:13:29.030
The item you requested!

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:31.410
Oh?

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:34.460
Hey, skinhead, get back! You'll turn into an old man!

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:54.680
All right then, about that reward...

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:55.020
Huh?

00:13:55.020 --> 00:13:57.560
Miss... Ichiko?

00:14:01.480 --> 00:14:02.780
Um... Er...

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:05.070
You know, the reward...

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:06.280
Next time, 'kay?

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:08.360
No! What! Why!

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:10.280
When's that?

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.290
Poor Ichiko.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:18.670
She possessed a power capable of granting anything she wanted...

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:23.300
But she didn't realize what
she really wanted until now.

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:26.550
But it's too late now,

00:14:26.880 --> 00:14:30.140
for I have appeared before thee.

00:14:30.510 --> 00:14:31.510
That aside...

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:36.020
I won't be satisfied 'til you're soup, you useless turtle!

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:40.020
No! You're inhuman! I mean, unholy!

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:51.570
Ouch!

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:53.280
Did you hear that?

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:57.540
Some innocent human just
stubbed his toe on the dresser.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:03.040
Because of Sakura Ichiko, innocent people are being exposed to Misfortune even as we speak.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:09.380
Are you listening to me, Momiji?!

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:14.890
I'm listening. I'm not slacking off.

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:19.560
These are special recreational activities designed to boost morale.

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:20.560
R-Really now?

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:22.520
Oh? Fukayama's next, who wants to sing?

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:23.860
Oh, me, me!

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:29.780
<i>Oh shit, the demon came back!</i>

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:38.080
Huh?

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:40.210
Man, that scared the pants off me.

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:43.460
But that was an unusually calm
reaction for Sakura Ichiko.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:44.710
Indeed.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:51.090
<i>Ever since she returned to normal,
her mind's been somewhere else.</i>

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:57.220
It's true.

00:15:57.220 --> 00:16:00.100
More like she's soulless.

00:16:00.560 --> 00:16:04.350
It also makes things difficult for me
when my opponent is like that, 24/7.

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:09.860
I see an opening and start my attack, but her Fortune kicks in right on time.

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:16.330
Like, come on, she still hasn't realized that
we replaced her slippers with steel ingots.

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:18.330
You're right. That's pretty serious.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:22.920
In that case, I will apply one of my shock remedies!

00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:26.790
Guess... who... it is!

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:33.050
Ve-Vegeta!

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:38.720
Huh, so nothing changed.

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:43.230
Baldy! I'll never forget your courage!

00:16:43.480 --> 00:16:46.610
All right! Now, just leave it to me!

00:16:51.490 --> 00:16:53.490
<i>You're too soft, Baldy.</i>

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:58.080
<i>It takes more than a little sexual harassment to get Miss Ichiko to reveal her true self.</i>

00:16:58.080 --> 00:17:01.410
Move, you stupid dog!

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:05.500
<i>Operation "The S in Sakura Ichiko is the S in BDSM!"</i>

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:05.920
<i>Huh?</i>

00:17:09.710 --> 00:17:10.380
Um...

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:13.170
Miss Ichiko?

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:14.840
<i>No! No!</i>

00:17:15.380 --> 00:17:16.840
<i>This isn't...</i>

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:20.310
This isn't Miss Ichiko!

00:17:21.180 --> 00:17:24.180
Momou!

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:28.900
<i>Our warriors fall one by one.</i>

00:17:28.900 --> 00:17:29.650
<i>Why you...</i>

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:33.570
<i>Looks like it's up to me.</i>

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:35.950
Five minutes left!

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:41.120
Be sure to check your answers if you have time!

00:17:44.750 --> 00:17:46.330
All right, pens down!

00:17:51.210 --> 00:17:52.710
C'mon, react <i>somehow</i>!

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:56.720
Damn it, and after I finally got Yamabuki to come help...

00:17:57.430 --> 00:17:59.590
And why isn't the class saying anything?

00:17:59.590 --> 00:18:03.640
They better not be thinking that I'm just doing weird things again.

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:06.440
<i>Binbouda's doing weird things again...</i>

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:08.230
Hm?

00:18:08.810 --> 00:18:11.440
I couldn't even sleep during the test...

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:12.230
Um...

00:18:12.230 --> 00:18:14.940
Hey, Tsu-Tsuwa—

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:16.950
Huh?

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:24.080
Oh? What was that just then?

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:26.960
I see, so that's how it is.

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.290
Has spring come for you already, Ichiko?!

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:32.250
If you don't say anything, you'll
never get your chance, you know!

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.300
Break out the champagne, dear!
This is a special occasion!

00:18:36.880 --> 00:18:39.220
Huh? Wait a sec...

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:49.980
Ichiko, you jerk!

00:18:50.310 --> 00:18:54.440
Well... First off, it's time for your report.

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:58.950
What the hell are you doing, slacking off again?!
Show some damn respect!

00:19:00.320 --> 00:19:01.700
So there you have it.

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:06.450
Get it, Momiji? Even I have my limits!

00:19:06.450 --> 00:19:11.540
If you keep this up, I'll switch you out for another God of Misfortune!

00:19:11.960 --> 00:19:14.840
Sure. That might be for the best.

00:19:16.130 --> 00:19:19.720
Did I come here to act the fool?

00:19:20.380 --> 00:19:24.720
It's not even annoying anymore. It's just pointless.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:38.530
God-fucking-dammit! This is so stupid!

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:43.370
What's wrong with me? Why do I feel so confused?!

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:48.700
And it's all because of this stupid handkerchief!

00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.710
<i>Yeah, so I accidentally held on to it,
but that's done and done!</i>

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:53.750
<i>I just need to give it back already!</i>

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:56.550
Here, you dropped this.

00:19:56.550 --> 00:19:57.250
Oh, thanks.

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:01.760
What'd you write your address on it for? You still a kid?

00:20:01.760 --> 00:20:07.260
But now I can't even talk to him properly because of everything that happened!

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:11.230
Oh, that's right. I should just leave it here and go.

00:20:11.560 --> 00:20:12.600
What're you doing?

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.400
<i>Oh shit!</i>

00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:20.400
<i>This is my chance! Just return it normally!</i>

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:22.280
He-he-he-he-he-he-he...

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:23.820
<i>What is she, a chicken?</i>

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:27.830
Is this mine? You came all the way for this?

00:20:28.910 --> 00:20:30.330
<i>Come on, say something...</i>

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:33.250
Wonder if Michiko dropped it...

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:37.750
<i>What the hell are you thinking?!</i>

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:40.590
Speaking of which, this is the second time you've brought back something I lost.

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:43.470
Thanks. Sorry about that.

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:46.220
"Sorry about that"?

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:50.060
That's right. That's fine.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:55.060
You <i>better</i> be thankful! See ya!

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:58.400
<i>What a woman...</i>

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:00.650
<i>I did it!</i>

00:21:01.030 --> 00:21:04.650
<i>I returned it! I returned it! I returned it!</i>

00:21:04.650 --> 00:21:07.530
Finally got that off my shoulders!

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:10.290
Wow, what an invigorating feeling!

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:14.830
Like putting on a fresh pair of panties, or the first day of a new year!

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:18.210
Everything feels so clear now!

00:21:20.170 --> 00:21:21.050
Huh...

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:22.800
Huh?

00:21:23.470 --> 00:21:24.720
What...

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:27.890
What the heck is this?!

00:21:29.510 --> 00:21:35.520
I might've been a bit under the weather, but I see <i>you</i> guys sure made yourselves at home!

00:21:36.310 --> 00:21:37.600
This raging torrent of anger...

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:39.610
Could... Could it be...

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:43.610
Yes! Ichiko's back to normal!

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:49.070
Yeah... I wouldn't have it any other way.

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:22.040
My substitute?! The hell are you talking about?

00:23:22.040 --> 00:23:23.750
Huh? But you said...

00:23:23.750 --> 00:23:26.210
I told you I'd be the one to do her in!

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:27.380
You going senile, hag?

00:23:27.380 --> 00:23:30.050
What's with that girl?!

00:23:30.470 --> 00:23:33.090
This week's <i>Nadeshiko ga!</i> has been canceled due to time constraints.

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:35.060
Please goddamn find her yourselves.

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:38.600
What? Canceled?!

00:23:38.600 --> 00:23:40.520
That's not right.

00:23:40.520 --> 00:23:45.070
That can't possibly be right! Noooo!
